\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Strong Early, Despite Fall In Overnight Rate \b0\par\par\uc2 370 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 1999\par 05:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is stronger early Monday, shrugging off what dealers see as a temporary dip in a key short-term rate below its U.S. counterpart. \par \par \uc2  Around 0315 GMT (11:15 p.m. EDT Sunday), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7488 against the U.S. dollar, compared with HK$7.7491 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 4.50%, compared with 4.75% late Friday, and 25 basis points below its U.S. counterpart. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they don't expect the overnight rate to stay below its U.S. counterpart, noting that the fall in both the overnight rate and in forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums reflect a return of confidence in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  "We see strength in the spot Hong Kong dollar, a local bank treasurer said. "Confidence has surged." \par \par \uc2  The treasurer noted that the spread between the spot rate and the so-called \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  guarantees to buy the Hong Kong dollar has widened to more than 20 basis points from just one basis point since the start of "phased devaluation" April 1. \par \par \uc2  That strength also reflects the market's confidence in the spot Hong Kong dollar, he said. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a British bank said even a 2.1% fall in the blue-chip Hang Seng Index hasn't phased the market, with some funds, which missed out on last week's three-day 7.6% rally, seeing the correction as an opportunity to buy when key stocks have fallen far enough. \par \par \uc2  In the forwards, the one-month premium is quoted at 13 points, down from 22 late Friday. The three-month premium is quoted at 85 points, compared with 95 points previously. The six-month premium is quoted at 260 points, down from 305. The one-year premium is quoted at 950 points, down from 1,100, marking the first time the one-year has strayed below 1,000 points since early January. \par \par \uc2  - By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2832 2336; sean.kennedy@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 12-04-99 \par \par \uc2  0349GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv4c02q48\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
