ightly stronger than HK$7.7491 earlier in the day and much stronger than the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Friday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate of HK$7.7509. \par \par \uc2  "The spot (\b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar) is expected to remain stable between HK$7.7480 and HK$7.7500 (per U.S. dollar)," Commonwealth Bank of Australia treasurer Andrew Fung said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 09-04-99 \par \par \uc2  1016GMT \par \par \uc2  1138 4201 55127 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv4902rp2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
