\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Stronger Midday On Inflow Of Overseas Funds \b0\par\par\uc2 349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 1999\par 06:24\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is trading stronger at midday Thursday, with overseas investment funds buying the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to enter the stock market. \par \par \uc2  With the Hang Seng Index hitting its highest levels of the year over the past two sessions, money is flowing from overseas through the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and destined for investment in stocks. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar is at HK$7.7488 per U.S. dollar at 0344 GMT (11:44 p.m. EDT Wednesday), higher than HK$7.7498 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In the middle of last week, most investors hedged and expected the local dollar to weaken and hit the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, which is moving at a rate of 0.0001-point per day. \par \par \uc2  But a surge in the home stock market to begin the week and a corresponding increase in Hong Kong dollar demand indicates overseas mutual funds are back in this market in a big way. \par \par \uc2  The spot exchange rate is stronger, as are short-term interbank interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The blue-chip index is quoted at 11,774.09 around 0344 GMT (11:44 p.m. EDT Wednesday), up 159.22 points from Wednesday's close. The index climbed 541.89 points Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The head of treasury at a domestic bank said the large size of transactions, coupled with their straightforwardness in the spot market, indicates a significant inflow of "hot money" into Hong Kong markets. He said the characteristics of trades in the past two sessions point to mutual funds needing local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to get into the stock market. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar may test as strong as HK$7.7480 later in the day, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Forward premiums are easing, another sign investors aren't worried about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk, despite renewed debate about a possible yuan devaluation. The one-year premium is down to 1,210 points from 1,270 points late Wednesday. The three-month premium is down to 105 points from 115 points. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-04-99 \par \par \uc2  0424GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv4802n1d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
