\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Stronger Early; High Short-Term Rates Help \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 1999\par 05:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is stronger early Wednesday, helped by high short-term interbank rates. \par \par \uc2  Around 0310 GMT (11:10 p.m. EDT Tuesday), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7497 against the U.S. dollar, compared with HK$7.7500 late Thursday. The U.S. dollar has traded between HK$7.7497 and HK$7.7505 so far Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  It's the first day of trading after the market closed for three trading days for holidays. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 5.75%, up from 5.50% late Thursday, the last day of trading. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market is relatively quiet early in the session. "This morning, the market is quiet and is range-trading," said a local bank treasurer. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with an Australian bank said he noted buying of the Hong Kong dollar in Australia and buying in Hong Kong from Singapore institutions. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market has shrugged off "phased devaluation" of the Hong Kong dollar by the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Under phased devaluation, which started on April 1, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level, at which the HKMA guarantees to buy \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars for U.S. dollars, will move by one basis point per day for 500 days until the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level hits HK$7.80 per U.S. dollar, the original level at which it was pegged in late 1983. \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the one-month premium is quoted at 42 points, from 55 late Thursday. The three-month premium is quoted at 130, down from 150. The six-month premium is at 380, down from 450. The one-year premium is quoted at 1,325, down from 1,450. \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2832 2336;sean.kennedy@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 07-04-99 \par \par \uc2  0345GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv4702nnr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
