\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Weaker Late After Some Institutions Test HKMA Mettle \b0\par\par\uc2 393 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 09:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is weaker against the U.S. dollar late Wednesday on the eve of "phased devaluation" by the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after some participants decided to test the HKMA's resolve by selling off the local unit. \par \par \uc2  Around 0655 GMT (1:55 a.m. EST), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7499 against the U.S. dollar, compared with HK$7.7489 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the movement isn't unexpected, given the HKMA's plan to let its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level - the level at which it guarantees it will buy Hong Kong dollars - move one basis point a day for 500 days, until the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reverts to HK$7.80, the level at which it was originally pegged in 1983. Since the late 1980s, the Hong Kong dollar has generally traded on the strong side of the peg. \par \par \uc2  Starting Apr. 1, the "phased devaluation" is intended to strengthen the local unit's peg to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar weakened after some participants sold the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar to push it close to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level, to see if the HKMA moved it in step with the 500-day "phased devaluation," a treasurer at a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  As a result, the HKMA bought about HK$775 million in the market, pushing up short-term rates, and some forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But dealers don't expect high drama in the spot market Thursday, despite the weakness in the current session. "Today, they (the HKMA) will support it at HK$7.7500. Tomorrow, they'll support it at HK$7.7501," an Australian dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong interbank offered rate is quoted at 6.00%, up from 5.25% late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the one-month premium is quoted at 48 points, up from 42 late Tuesday. The three-month premium is quoted at 150 points, compared with 140 points previously. The six-month premium is quoted at 450 points, up from 430 previously. The one-year premium is quoted at 1,430 points, down from 1,450 previously. \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2832 2336; sean.kennedy@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 31-03-99 \par \par \uc2  0736GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3v02i63\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
