\par\par \b \uc2  HK Govt Silent On Alleged Futures "Front-Running" By Broker \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 18:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong government Tuesday refused to say whether the Securities and Futures Commission is investigating a broker for alleged misconduct related to its attempt last year to defend the local market from a speculative attack. \par \par \uc2  Since last week, the government has been under pressure to comment on an unconfirmed newspaper report that alleged a futures broker used by the government bought stock index futures with prior knowledge that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was about to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the market - a practice known as "front-running." \par \par \uc2  In response to written questions from Dow Jones Newswires, the government said the securities regulator is bound by law to keeps its investigations confidential and indicated it would not divulge information concerning SFC actions. \par \par \uc2  It also confirmed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  began \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Hang Seng Index futures market on Aug. 13, a day earlier than it had previously said. \par \par \uc2  The government didn't explain why it took nearly nine months to acknowledge the real starting date of the HKMA's two-week anti-speculative market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying only that it "did not consider it necessary to report on these preparatory details." \par \par \uc2  For the first time, the government said the HKMA bought 491 August Hang Seng Index futures in the last 20 minutes of trading on Aug. 13, or 1.98% of the contract turnover of the day. It did so to test market conditions as speculators sold index futures and Hong Kong dollar forwards short in a bid to test the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peg to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The test was also to gauge "the extent and sources of selling pressure on the trading floor of the Hong Kong Futures Exchange" and to check its command structure, internal systems and settlement procedures in preparation for a bigger battle with speculators in the days ahead. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 30-03-99 \par \par \uc2  1613GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3u02fy7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
