\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Late Weaker But Trapped In Range \b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 09:20\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is fractionally weaker in a lackluster market, but still range-bound in the absence of news to provide direction. \par \par \uc2  Around 0700 GMT (2:00 a.m. EST), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7490 against the U.S. dollar, compared with HK$7.7489 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market is quiet, with many players sidelined ahead of a long weekend. The market will close for three trading days from Friday when a Chinese holiday coincides with the Easter break. \par \par \uc2  While the spot Hong Kong dollar is a touch weaker, dealers said it's not going to go anywhere fast. \par \par \uc2  "It has been very stable and relatively firm," said a local bank treasurer. The spot Hong Kong dollar's weakened earlier this month when low short-term interbank rates caused a cash outflow in search of higher-yielding U.S. dollar assets, pushing the Hong Kong dollar close to HK$7.7500, a level thought to be a trigger for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Short-term interbank rates are also steady, with the normally volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate quoted at 5.00%, unchanged from late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they don't expect the introduction of "phased" devaluation of the Hong Kong dollar from April 1, which the HKMA announced last September, to spark volatility. "Frankly speaking, I'm not expecting anything special to happen," one dealer commented. \par \par \uc2  Nor do dealers expect the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee to cut rates at its meeting Tuesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the forward \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, the one-month premium is\par quoted at 37 points from 33 late Friday. The three-month premium is\par quoted at 135 points, up from 125 points. The six-month premium is at\par 440 points, up from 430. The one-year premium is at 1,400 points, down\par from 1,440.\par   -By Sean Kennedy (852) 2832 2336;sean.kennedy@cor.dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 29-03-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0720GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3t02exs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
