\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Stronger Early; Boosted By Higher Overnight Rate \b0\par\par\uc2 400 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 04:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is stronger early Tuesday, helped by a further rise in the volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate eliminating the differential over its U.S. counterpart that sparked outflows last week. \par \par \uc2  Around 0220 GMT (9:20 p.m. Monday EST), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7493 against the U.S. dollar, from HK$7.7497 late Monday. However, it has only traded between HK$7.7492 and HK$74.94 so far Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a British bank said the Hong Kong dollar is buoyed by the rise in short-term rates, noting that the overnight rate is now almost double the 2.75% level it was quoted at one week earlier. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate is quoted at 5.125%, compared with 4.75% late Monday, and significantly higher than its U.S. counterpart at about 4.75%. Low short-term rates last week undermined the Hong Kong dollar as money flowed out into higher-yielding U.S. money market instruments. \par \par \uc2  However, a dealer with an Australian bank said trade remains extremely thin, and dealers generally don't expect major movement ahead of next week's Federal Open Market Committee meeting Tuesday and the start of phased devaluation by the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Following a sustained attack on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar last year and government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, the HKMA said it planned to let the Hong Kong dollar move back to the original pegged level against the U.S. dollar of HK$7.80 per U.S. dollar in a "phased" devaluation. \par \par \uc2  Dealers added that the market is also focusing on the performance of the Japanese yen for any signs it's about to go into free fall against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums have been pushed up by the higher short-term rates. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the forwards, the one-month premium is quoted at 32 points from 23\par late Monday. The three-month premum is quoted at 150 points, up from 135\par points. The six-month premium is quoted at 480 points, up from 445. The\par one-year premium is quoted at 1,560 points, up from 1,460.\par   -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2832 2336;sean.kennedy@cor.dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 23-03-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0308GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3n029wf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
