\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Slightly Stronger Early As Liquidity Tightens \b0\par\par\uc2 394 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 04:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is stronger early Monday after short-term rates rose on a fall in overall banking liquidity. \par \par \uc2  Around 0200 GMT (9:00 p.m. EST Sunday), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7495 against the U.S. dollar, compared with HK$7.7499 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the aggregate balance, which commercial banks hold to clear \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions with the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , will fall to HK$2.91 billion Tuesday, when an outflow of about US$170 million equivalent is settled. A commercial bank bought the US$170 million equivalent from the HKMA late Friday. Rates are now starting to reflect the tighter liquidity. \par \par \uc2  "Short-term rates have rebounded from last week's lows," said a dealer with an Australian bank, noting that short-term rates had dived last week on anticipation of a rate cut Friday which failed to materialize. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong interbank offered rate is quoted at 4.50%, compared with 4.25% late Friday. \par \par \uc2  With the overnight rate at this level or higher, switching into U.S. dollars to take advantage of an overnight rate of 4.75% has lost its appeal, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expect the Hong Kong dollar to hold its own for the moment but it may weaken from April 1. "This is because market people expect when next month the HKMA moves the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate one pip (0.0001 point) per day, ... the U.S. dollar will test the upside," a dealer with a U.S. bank said. \par \par \uc2  The HKMA is believed to have HK$7.75 as its trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar. Last year, the HKMA said it would allow the Hong Kong dollar to weaken to HK$7.80 per U.S. dollar under a "phased" devaluation. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the forward \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, the one-month premium is\par quoted at 20 points from 14 late Friday. The three-month premium is\par quoted at 145, up from 105. The six-month premium is quoted at 450, up\par from 420. The one-year premium is quoted at 1,500, up from 1,430.\par    -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2832 2336;sean.kennedy@cor.dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 22-03-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0316GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3m026ay\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
