\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Steady Late; Mkt Awaits Outcome Of Key Bk Meeting \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 09:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is in the doldrums late Friday as the market waits for the outcome of a meeting of the Hong Kong Association of Banks (HKAB) and a possible cut in a key benchmark interest rate. \par \par \uc2  Around 0725 GMT (2:25 a.m. EST), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7499 against the U.S. dollar, barely changed from HK$7.7498 late Thursday and unchanged from early Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said nobody wants to do too much until the HKAB meeting ends sometime after 0835 GMT (3:35 a.m. EST) in case the Association decides to cut the deposit rate by 25 basis points, freeing the way for individual banks to cut their best lending rates. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a British bank said a rate cut is fully factored into short-term rates now, but dealers generally felt a rate cut later Friday would be premature. \par \par \uc2  The spot Hong Kong dollar is at the weak end of its range, and is expected to come under further pressure if interest rates fall. It's currently close to HK$7.7500 to the U.S. dollar, seen as a trigger point for defense by \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Expectations of a rate cut have pulled down forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums, particularly in the three-month maturity. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the forwards, the one-month premium is quoted at 14 points, from 15\par late Thursday. The three-month premium is quoted at 105 points, compared\par with 130 points previously. The six-month premium is quoted at 420\par points, down from 450 previously. The one-year premium is quoted at\par 1,430 points, down from 1,550 previously.\par    -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2832 2336;sean.kennedy@cor.dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-03-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0802GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3j027ad\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
