\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Weak Early; Forwards Dn On Possible Rate Cut \b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 04:19\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums are lower early Friday as players brace for a possible rate cut later in the session even though many think such a cut will only erode the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  Around 0240 GMT (9:40 p.m. EST Thursday), the Hong Kong dollar was quoted at HK$7.7499 against the U.S. dollar, compared with HK$7.7498 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is perilously close to HK$7.7500, a trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the local unit, but forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums are lower, reflecting growing expectations of a rate cut. \par \par \uc2  In the forwards, the one-month premium is at 14 points from 15 late Thursday. The three-month is quoted at 105 points, down from 130. The six-month rate is at 420 points, from 450. The one-year premium is at 1,500 points, down from 1,550. \par \par \uc2  "Some people in the market are speculating there will be a rate cut," said a local bank treasurer, adding that he thinks the government wants rates to fall ahead of April 20, when it resumes its program of land auctions. \par \par \uc2  "There's a 30% to 40% chance of a rate cut," said another bank treasurer. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers think a cut in the deposit rate later Friday will accelerate cash outflows into higher-yielding U.S. dollar money market instruments. \par \par \uc2  This would force the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the local unit by selling U.S. dollars and buying Hong Kong dollars, causing a cash crunch in Hong Kong and squeezing banks' margins. \par \par \uc2  Stock market traders said earlier this week that it's probably not appropriate to cut the deposit rate given the recent strength of the Hang Seng Index and the weakness of the spot Hong Kong dollar. A director at one local brokerage said a rate cut should be reserved for when the stock market is in danger of collapsing. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2832 2336;\par    sean.kennedy@cor.dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-03-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0319GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3j026fm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
