\par\par \b \uc2  HK Overnight Money At Intraday High, Local Stk Mkt Fall Eyed \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 09:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong's overnight interbank rate has inched higher from morning levels, in quiet trading late Thursday, with banks nervously eying a steep fall in the local stock market. \par \par \uc2  Lenders are concerned that Thursday's sharp decline in the Hang Seng Index may trigger an outflow of funds into U.S. dollars. The HSI closed down 2.5%, at 10659.32 points. \par \par \uc2  Hot money from overseas investors has fueled much of the stock market's gains in the past few weeks, and a quick shift out of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could add to the recent pressure on the Hong Kong dollar spot rate. \par \par \uc2  The local unit has recently been flirting with HK$7.7500, a level that has, in the past, prompted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Earlier this week, some participants in the interbank market were moving into U.S. dollars, because of extremely low Hong Kong dollar interbank rates. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate is quoted at 4.0%, up from 3.5% in morning dealings, but still lower than late Wednesday's 4.25%. The rate fell as low as 1%-2% earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  The three-month rate is at 5.625%, a touch higher than its morning level of 5.5%, but unchanged from late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said weakness in the Hong Kong dollar could dissuade local banks from cutting their prime lending rates Friday. Last week, the chairman of the Hong Kong Association of Banks said there was room to cut local deposit and lending rates, but a stable environment was needed. \par \par \uc2  Around 0800 GMT (3:00 a.m. EST), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7498 to the U.S. dollar, little changed from HK$7.7499 recorded late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 18-03-99 \par \par \uc2  0843GMT \par \par \uc2  4178 5096 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3i023c8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
