\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Range-Bound Late Morning,Still Pressured By Low Rates \b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 04:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is trapped near a key support level late-morning Thursday, but the overnight rate is higher, though not enough to stem cash outflows in search of higher-yielding U.S. dollar securities. \par \par \uc2  Around 0300 GMT (10:00 p.m. Wednesday EST), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7498 against the U.S. dollar, compared with HK$7.7499 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar has traded in a range of HK$7.7495 to HK$7.7497 so far Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong interbank offered rate is quoted at 3.375%, up from 3.00% late Wednesday and well up from its level of 2.50% late Tuesday, but not enough to strengthen the local unit, which has recently been flirting with HK$7.75, seen as a trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "People are still chasing yield in U.S. dollars," said a senior dealer at a British bank, adding that this is unlikely to change in the short term. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said interest rates now appear fully to factor in a 25-basis-point cut in the deposit rate as early as Friday, although most think it's not yet time to cut rates. A director at a local brokerage firm also ruled out a rate cut this Friday, saying it's more appropriate to cut rates when the stock market is languishing. The blue-chip Hang Seng Index has gained 11% so far this month alone, despite relatively high real interest rates. \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the one-month premium is quoted at 15 points, down from 17 late Wednesday. The three-month premium is quoted at 130 points, unchanged. The six-month premium is quoted at 460 points, down from 470 previously. The one-year premium is quoted at 1,575 points, up from 1,550 previously. \par \par \uc2  - By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2832 2336; sean.kennedy@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 18-03-99 \par \par \uc2  0334GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3i0223g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
