\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Weak Near Midday, Flirts With HK$7.75 \b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 04:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is under pressure midday Wednesday, pushing toward a traditionally key resistance level as low prevailing short-term interest rates maul the local unit. \par \par \uc2  Around 0315 GMT (10:15 p.m. Tuesday EST), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7499 against the U.S. dollar, compared with HK$7.7496 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A treasurer with a local bank said the local unit actually traded at HK$7.7502, breaking through HK$7.7500, seen as a trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , before pulling back to HK$7.7499. \par \par \uc2  However, he said the HKMA isn't likely to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the transactions aren't significant. "Why should they (the HKMA) do anything if the amount is not that big? Why should they call them on it?" he said, noting that the planned phased devaluation of the Hong Kong dollar also makes the HK$7.75 level less sensitive than in the past. \par \par \uc2  Short-term interest rates remain low, although slightly up from Tuesday, and dealers said prevailing short-term rates now fully factor in a possible rate cut by the Hong Kong Association of Banks at its weekly meeting Friday. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong interbank offered rate is quoted at 3.375%, compared with 2.75% late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums are generally higher, in line with the slight bounce in interbank rates. \par \par \uc2  In the forwards, the one-month premium is quoted at 10 points, down from 11 late Tuesday. The three-month premium is quoted at 120 points, compared with 107 points. The six-month premium is quoted at 445 points, up from 425 previously. The one-year premium is quoted at 1,520 points, up from 1,475 previously. \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2832 2336; sean.kennedy@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 17-03-99 \par \par \uc2  0342GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3h022mr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
