\par\par \b \uc2  HKMA changes Exchange Fund asset allocations. \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 11:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, March 3 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) said on Wednesday it will cut the Exchange Fund's local equity portfolio to five percent from 17 percent as market conditions permit. \par \par \uc2  "The pace of re-balancing the asset mix of the Exchange Fund ... will obviously depend on market conditions and may take some time," said Joseph Yam, Chief Executive of the HKMA. \par \par \uc2  "The government is not in a hurry to offload the shares and is confident that the Exchange Fund will take great care in executing the disposal programme in an orderly manner without disrupting the market," he added. \par \par \uc2  The change is part of an overall asset reallocation strategy approved by the Exchange Fund Advisory Committee. \par \par \uc2  Under the new investment plan investment benchmarks have changed as follows: \par \par \uc2  The benchmark for bonds is now 80 percent, down from 90 percent. The benchmark for equities is 20 percent (five percent Hong Kong equities), down from 10 percent. \par \par \uc2  For \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the new target is a holding of 80 percent US$-bloc \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , 15 percent European-bloc \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and five percent Japanese Yen. The previous benchmark targets were 70 percent, 20 percent and 10 percent respectively. \par \par \uc2  The goal of the new investment mix is to preserve capital, ensure the monetary base is fully backed by highly liquid, short term U.S.-dollar denominated assets as well as maintaining enough liquidity to preserve monetary and financial stability, according to the announcement. Following the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  stock market last August, the Exchange Fund acquired a portfolio of Hong Kong equities which account for about 17 percent of the fund's total assets. \par \par \uc2  As at December 31, 1998, assets of the fund totalled HK$910 billion. The new benchmark of a five percent allocation to Hong Kong equities means that HK$46 billion of the current HK$150 billion equity portfolio will be kept as a long term investment. \par \par \uc2  - Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2568-6773; Fax (852) 2845-0636 \par \par \uc2  - Email: hongkong.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv33024ie\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
