\par\par \b \uc2  US/HK forwards firmer at open on overseas buying. \b0\par\par\uc2 214 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 1999\par 03:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    OPEN\tab      PREVIOUS CLOSE\par     HK$ SPOT\tab    7.7473/83\tab 7.7478/88\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     FORWARDS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Three month\tab 220-250\tab   200-220\par     Six-month\tab   720-770\tab   630-680\par     One-year\tab    1,850-1,950    1,750-1,850\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INTERBANK RATE (IN PERCENTAGE)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Overnight\tab   5.25-5.75\tab 5.25-5.50\par     Three-month\tab 5.75-6.25\tab 5.88-6.12\par     Six-month\tab   6.63-7.13\tab 6.62-6.88\par     One-year\tab    7.25-7.75\tab 7.38-7.62.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Feb 25 (Reuters) - US/HK forwards were up at the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par open on Thursday as jitters about Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spurred\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign-based fund houses to short sell the Hong Kong dollar,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But the scale of the short sales was modest, and buying in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forwards was limited to the longer end.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Brazil's real slumped another 2 percent on Wednesday to close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at its second weakest level ever despite \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cut down on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's volatility.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar spot held firm, while short-term\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interbank rates remained steady, indicating that the market was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par calm and concerns about Brazil had not caused undue market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par nervousness, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  - Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2847 4039; Fax 2845 0636.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv2p03x85\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
