\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Weak Late, Hit By Last-Minute Pre-Holiday Jitters \b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 1999\par 08:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is weaker late Friday, amid last-minute buying of U.S. dollars ahead of next week's Chinese New Year holiday and renewed bidding in the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Around 0716 GMT (02:16 a.m. EST), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7498 against the U.S. dollar, weaker than the HK$7.7485 quoted late Thursday. It has traded between HK$7.7492 and HK$7.7500 so far Friday. \par \par \uc2  At one point, the Hong Kong dollar actually traded at HK$7.7500, once seen as a trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the territory's quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but no longer a defense point now that the HKMA is letting the Hong Kong dollar revert to its HK$7.80 level over time through a phased devaluation. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said sentiment is skittish, particularly ahead of next week's holiday, which will see the territory's stock market only trade a half-session Monday, before closing for the next three days. \par \par \uc2  "People are scared of being short (of U.S. dollars) before a long holiday," said a dealer with a British bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there's a significant increase in hedging over the next week, which is pushing up short-term forwards to as high as 20 points for overnight cover, or an effective cost of 7%. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in the forwards, the one-month is quoted at 90 points, up from 42 late Thursday. The three-month premium is at 290 points, up from 210 points. The six-month premium is at 800 points, up from 660. The one-year premium is at 2,000 points, up from 1,900, its first breach of 2,000 in the past 10 trading sessions. \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2832 2336; sean.kennedy@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 12-02-99 \par \par \uc2  0753GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv2c017rp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
