\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Steady Late; Forwards Dn As Yuan Concerns Ease \b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 1999\par 08:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is steady late Tuesday, as investors take comfort from Chinese Premier Zhu Rongji's comments that the mainland doesn't plan to devalue its yuan. \par \par \uc2  Around 0730 GMT (2:30 a.m. EST), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7490 against the U.S. dollar, unchanged from late Monday and early Tuesday. The Hong Kong dollar has only traded at HK$7.7490 during the session. \par \par \uc2  "The spot market is very quiet," said a local bank treasurer, adding that the focus remains on the more choppy forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, where premiums are falling as some players took profit during the session, dragging them back down. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they believe the spot Hong Kong dollar traded at HK$7.7500 to the U.S. dollar early in Australian trade, where the thinner liquidity makes it easier to move the market. The HK$7.7500 is normally seen as a trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said sentiment has improved markedly from the previous session, which was marked by fears that China might be backing away from earlier promises not to devalue the yuan. However, Zhu's comments late Monday allayed those fears. \par \par \uc2  The most active trading was in the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, where the one-year premium looks set to fall below 2,000 points for the first time in a week. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the forward \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, the one-month premium is\par quoted at 70 points, from 130 late Monday. The three-month premium\par premium is quoted at 330 points, compared with 470 points previously.\par The six-month premium is quoted at 850 points, down from 1,200\par previously. The one-year premium is quoted at 2,175, down from 2,700\par previously.\par    -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2832 2336;sean.kennedy@cor.dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 26-01-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0753GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1q00ll7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
