\par\par \b \uc2  HKMA to complete Exchange Fund review near end Q1. \b0\par\par\uc2 235 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 1999\par 11:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Jan 19 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday a review of the investment strategy of the Land Fund and Exchange Fund would be completed at around the end of the first quarter or the start of the second quarter. \par \par \uc2  "The work is expected to be completed at around the end of the first quarter or the beginning of the second quarter," a spokesman told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong government has said its long-term strategy regarding its holdings of Hong Kong equities would be examined by the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of an overall review on asset allocation in the management of the Exchange Fund. \par \par \uc2  Last November, the government said it would amalgamate the assets of the Land Fund, which holds proceeds from government land sales, with its Exchange Fund, which provides backing for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peg to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  After the merger, the Hong Kong equity portfolio held in the Land Fund would be passed to Exchange Fund Investment Ltd (EFIL), a company formed to manage the HK$118 billion (US$15.2 billion) worth of Hong Kong blue chips which the government bought during a two-week stock market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign in August. \par \par \uc2  - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  Newsroom (852) 2843 6345; Fax (852) 2845 0636 \par \par \uc2  - Email: hongkong.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1j06d9f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoa