\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Weakens Late As Rates Stay Low; Bearishness Persists \b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 1998\par 09:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is weaker late Tuesday as a combination of low interbank rates and bearishness on the local unit's long-term outlook take their toll. \par \par \uc2  Around 0748 GMT (2:48 a.m. EST), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7482 against the U.S. dollar, weaker than the HK$7.7476 quoted late Monday. The local unit has traded between HK$7.7475 and HK$7.7485 so far Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Hong Kong dollar has been under pressure since the surprise 25 basis point rate cut last week by the Hong Kong Association of Banks. That has helped keep the overnight rate down around 4.0%, and interbank rates are expected to maintain recent lows for the next few weeks. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a local bank said he expects the Hong Kong dollar to be hit by any stock market weakness, with any falls in the Hang Seng Index likely to result in cash outflows, undermining the spot Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there's a general expectation that the Hong Kong dollar will continue to ease, pushing towards HK$7.7500, which was formerly seen as a trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, since the HKMA's announcement earlier this year that it would allow a phased devaluation of the Hong Kong dollar down to HK$7.80 per U.S. dollar, attention is focused on what will happen if or when it tests HK$7.7500. \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the one-month premium is quoted at six points, up from two late Monday. The three-month premium is quoted at 105 points, compared with 120 points previously. The six-month premium is quoted at 520 points, down from 550 Monday. The one-year premium is quoted at 1,750 points, down from 1,800 previously. \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2802 7002; skennedy@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-12-98 \par \par \uc2  0811GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duc801vwj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
