\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA MARKETS-Regional stocks down with the Dow. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Christopher Kaufman \par \uc2 1,035 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 1998\par 11:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      HONG KONG, Dec 1 (Reuters) - Asian stocks were hit hard on \par \par \uc2  Tuesday by the fall on Wall Street but traders and strategists \par \par \uc2  were not ready just yet to call the markets a strong sell. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in very narrow ranges, suggesting that \par \par \uc2  funds have not started to flee equities. \par \par \uc2      FINDING THE LIQUIDITY \par \par \uc2      The heaviest selling pressure began after Hong Kong's Hang \par \par \uc2  Seng index opened and promptly lost more than three percent of \par \par \uc2  its value. But dealers were not entirely convinced the region's \par \par \uc2  falls were the start of a major correction. \par \par \uc2  "This could be the start of a much needed and well earned \par \par \uc2  consolidation," said Miles Remington, head of institutional \par \par \uc2  sales at SG Asia. \par \par \uc2      "(But) the volumes have not really been around to \par \par \uc2  constitute a real sell off," he said. \par \par \uc2      "Hopefully, we are in the hands of other markets globally," \par \par \uc2  he said, echoing a view that even a 2.3 percent sell-off on \par \par \uc2  Wall Street could not be as bad for the market as a seven \par \par \uc2  percent fall in Hong Kong's GDP in the third quarter, recorded \par \par \uc2  on Friday. \par \par \uc2      "We're not seeing many investors (selling), it's mostly \par \par \uc2  traders taking profit," said a head trader at a European bank. \par \par \uc2      "Lots of books are closed already, job losses are already \par \par \uc2  decided, there's no need for people to step up and take new \par \par \uc2  positions," he said. \par \par \uc2      But even if a sharp correction does not come from the U.S., \par \par \uc2  Asian markets are not seen enjoying much foreign interest. \par \par \uc2      "For the next 12 months at least, the major source of new \par \par \uc2  liquidity for these markets will continue to be through the \par \par \uc2  public account," said Marshall Mays, chief strategist at Nikko \par \par \uc2  Securities in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  "The expectation of the real money coming from the private \par \par \uc2  credit sector is still a long way off," he told Reuters \par \par \uc2  Television on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG TECHNICALLY NUMBER ONE \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong retained its place at the top of the Heritage \par \par \uc2  Foundation's Index of Economic Freedom for 1999, but in name \par \par \uc2  only. The think-tank blamed \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its \par \par \uc2  stock market in August as the chief reason the territory has \par \par \uc2  lost out to rival Singapore in real results. \par \par \uc2  The 1999 index was completed on June 30. Hong Kong fell \par \par \uc2  from the number one spot in August when the government bought \par \par \uc2  HK$118 billion (US$15.2 billion) in shares to drive off \par \par \uc2  speculators. \par \par \uc2  IMF-ASSISTED NATIONS GET LETTERS IN ORDER \par \par \uc2  Details of IMF letters of intent with Indonesia and \par \par \uc2  Thailand were released while Korea moved closer to plans to \par \par \uc2  repay its Fund loans. \par \par \uc2  While few analysts saw any reason to expect a problem with \par \par \uc2  the disbursement of funds to Indonesia or Thailand, some \par \par \uc2  questioned the clarity the Indonesian letter would provide. \par \par \uc2  "This represents what you might call a process of examining \par \par \uc2  what's inside a box by sticking a series of needles into it," \par \par \uc2  said Mays. \par \par \uc2  "Each of the letters of intent is an attempt to report on \par \par \uc2  what has been done ... in reality, of course, the \par \par \uc2  accomplishments have so far substantially under-performed the \par \par \uc2  expectations, as one would expect with a society in such a \par \par \uc2  drastic depression as Indonesia is," he said. \par \par \uc2      Thailand's letter included a projection for a better than \par \par \uc2  expected one percent rise in GDP for 1999. \par \par \uc2      The letter also said Thai foreign reserves next year would \par \par \uc2  rise to $32 billion from $28 billion seen this year. \par \par \uc2       Meanwhile, Korea was preparing to host a group of IMF \par \par \uc2  officials Wednesday to discuss repayment of IMF's aid loans. \par \par \uc2      A finance ministry official said repayment of $2.73 billion \par \par \uc2  in aid loans maturing by the end of this year would be \par \par \uc2  discussed, as well as $2 billion coming due between January and \par \par \uc2  February. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  QUIET - MORE RUPIAH STRENGTH EXPECTED \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders were watching the December holiday period \par \par \uc2  roll quietly closer, with less and less business being done on \par \par \uc2  the already thinned regional \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Traders were generally unwilling to pick a favorite trade \par \par \uc2  in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but some thought the rupiah might find \par \par \uc2  some more upside before the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  In Hong Kong, Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Syahril \par \par \uc2  Sabirin said the rupiah could strengthen to 7,000 or 6,500 per \par \par \uc2  dollar and there was more room for interest rates to ease. \par \par \uc2      Change on the day \par \par \uc2   