\par\par \b \uc2  HK's Hang Seng Index/SG -2: Sees Wealth Destruction >U.HSB \b0\par\par\uc2 360 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 1998\par 06:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SG's baseline forecast for the blue-chip Hang Seng Index could be too low if there are no earnings downgrades, which would give the index a fair value of less than 9500. If there is a larger-than-expected collapse in earnings, fair value could be as low as 3300, the report said. \par \par \uc2  In terms of market sector, SG said it is overall neutral on bank stocks, recommending sale of Bank of East Asia Ltd. (BKEAY) and holding HSBC Holdings PLC (U.HSB). But it is bearish on property developers, conglomerates and telecommunication companies. It is "overweight" utilities as the safest plays. \par \par \uc2  "A powerful economic adjustment is underway, crunching wages, rentals and prices of goods and services," the report said. \par \par \uc2  "The scale of wealth destruction implied feeds back into corporate and banking sector fundamentals, ravaging earnings and balance sheets. Expect substantial earnings downgrades in 1999," according to the reports. \par \par \uc2  The firm said that U.S. interest rates are falling but that Hong Kong rates will retain a high spread over them, and that real rates will remain at a much more positive level than has been seen in the Special Administrative Region for a long time. It forecasts that three-month Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate will average 6.13% in 1999, which compares with Monday's Hibor fixing of 6.70089%, with a premium of 2.38 percentage points above comparable U.S. levels. \par \par \uc2  Leading the list of risks that will keep Hong Kong's interest rates high is "changing policy behavior," with the report saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's August stock market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "was a shock." The report said concerns about a devaluation of the Chinese yuan will return in 2000 and there will be continued attacks on the Hong Kong dollar, but the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg will be retained "by default." \par \par \uc2  "A return to high growth is not likely until around 2001 at the earliest," according to the 29-page report from SG researchers. \par \par \uc2  -James T. Areddy; jareddy@ap.org; 852.2802.7002 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 09-11-98 \par \par \uc2  0557GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917dub900x9p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
