\par\par \b \uc2  HK Hibor Higher Late As Mkt Eyes Forecast HK$ Outflow \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 1998\par 09:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong interbank rates are mostly higher late Monday as the market nervously eyes a forecast HK$1.82 billion outflow from the territory's banking system later in the week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say the market has been almost paralyzed by concern over the outflow, which has already been transacted, but won't be settled until Thursday under Hong Kong's T+2 settlement system. Hong Kong markets will be closed Wednesday for a public holiday. \par \par \uc2  "The market is empty," with almost no deals being completed, said a dealer at a local bank. He noted that bid/offer spreads have widened to around 50 basis points across the curve, reflecting the market jitters. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 4.75%, down from 6% late in the previous session. But the benchmark three-month rate is 7%, up from 6.25% late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Market participants were divided as to whether the Thursday outflow, and a smaller HK$78.0 million shrinkage expected Wednesday, were due to commercial transactions or were part of an attempt by the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is hovering near the key level of HK$7.75 to the U.S. dollar. The HKMA is known to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar hits that level in the spot market. \par \par \uc2  Around 0823 GMT (3:23 a.m. EST), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7497 to the U.S. dollar, weaker than HK$7.7495 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  However, several dealers said they believed the outflows were due to commercial transactions by Japanese and other banks in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  The HKMA declined to comment on whether it was active in the markets Monday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 26-10-98 \par \par \uc2  0834GMT \par \par \uc2  1085 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duaq00h4d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
