\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Weaker Midday; Low Interbank Rates Pressure  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 1998\par 04:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar spot rate is weaker in moderate trade midday Monday, under pressure from low interbank rates, market participants said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0315 GMT (10:15 p.m. EDT), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7499 against the U.S. dollar, compared with late Friday's closing level of HK$7.7495. The Hong Kong dollar has traded in a range of HK$7.7495 and HK$7.7499 so far Monday. \par \par \uc2  "We are seeing some short covering this morning (pushing) the exchange rate close to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  point of the MA (\b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," said a money trader with an Australian bank. The HKMA is said to support the local unit when it gets too close to its target level of HK$7.7500. \par \par \uc2  "It's a sign that the local interest rates must be too low at this level," said the trader, adding that trading activity has picked up from last week. \par \par \uc2  Another money trader with a local bank said that most market participants feel that interbank rates have hit bottom, and so they are trying to lock in rates now. In addition, month-end book closing demand is also putting added pressure on the local unit, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 4.50%, down from 6.00% late Friday. The three-month rate is 6.625%, up slightly from 6.25% late Friday. For more Hibor news, please refer to Telerate page [1085]. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong's overnight rate is below the equivalent U.S. Fed Funds target rate of 5.0%, prompting investors to buy U.S. dollars in the short term, and buy back the local unit in the future. As a result, Hong Kong interbank rates and forward premiums have risen, traders said. \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the three-month premium is quoted at 285 points, compared with 230 points previously. The six-month premium is quoted at 915 points, up from 825 previously. The one-year premium is quoted at 2,600 points, up from 2,550 previously. \par \par \uc2  -By Belinda Rabano; (852) 2802-7002; belinda.rabano@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 26-10-98 \par \par \uc2  0343GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duaq00g7d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
