\par\par \b \uc2  HK Hibor Higher Late On Scramble For Weekend Funds \b0\par\par\uc2 253 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 1998\par 11:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong interbank rates are higher late Friday as market participants scramble to lock in funds over the weekend, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 6.00% late Friday, up sharply from from 1.5% late in the previous session. But the three-month rate is only marginally higher, at 6.25% compared with 6.0% previously. \par \par \uc2  "Borrowers are eager to cover their positions" ahead of the weekend, said a dealer at a Chinese bank in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  But that's probably just a temporary situation, he added, and rates are expected to resume their recent rock-bottom levels next week. \par \par \uc2  Low interbank rates had been putting pressure on the Hong Kong dollar, as investors exited the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take advantage of higher U.S.-dollar returns. \par \par \uc2  Late Friday, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still hovering near HK$7.75 against the U.S. dollar, a level known to spark \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Around 0935 GMT (5:35 a.m. EDT), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7495, slightly weaker compared to HK$7.7492 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say the market wasn't too disappointed with the Hong Kong Association of Banks' decision earlier Friday to leave deposit rates unchanged, as few participants expected a rate cut after the association trimmed rates by 25 basis points last week. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 23-10-98 \par \par \uc2  0951GMT \par \par \