\par\par \b \uc2  HKMA Yam To Propose Releasing Minutes From Some Meetings \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 1998\par 07:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chief Executive Joseph Yam said in a speech delivered late Tuesday that he will propose releasing some of the minutes from meetings of a sub-committee on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -board \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I shall shortly be making a proposal to the financial secretary initially for the minutes of the sub-committee, other than those concerning market-sensitive issues, to be published, with an appropriate time lag," Yam said. \par \par \uc2  The group was set up to advise the Exchange Fund Advisory Committee, the de facto board of directors managing Hong Kong's reserves and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board, on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -board matters. \par \par \uc2  But the move to release the minutes isn't likely to drastically increase transparency of the inner workings of Hong Kong's monetary management, even though Yam suggested minutes of the Advisory Committee itself might be released as well at some later date. \par \par \uc2  Yam said that, since Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system rules out an independent monetary policy in the territory, there is little to reveal. \par \par \uc2  "We do not have a system whereby the HKMA has to take discretionary decisions to determine interest rates or to specify monetary targets," he said. "There has therefore not been a need for a mechanism for public scrutiny of discretionary decisions because there is nothing to scrutinize." \par \par \uc2  However, the HKMA has come under fire recently for manipulating interest rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to support \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , despite the existence of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -board system that is supposed to make such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unnecessary or even impossible. And in August, the HKMA along with the government, took the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  another step further by buying an estimated HK$15.00 billion in local shares in an attempt to squeeze speculators out of the territory's markets. \par \par \uc2  -By Jeffrey Timmermans; (852) 2802-7002; jeffrey.timmermans@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-10-98 \par \par \uc2  0531GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917dual00ab8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
