\par\par \b \uc2  HK Late Hibor Falls; Encouraged By Japanese Rally \b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 1998\par 11:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong interbank rates are sharply lower late Wednesday, helped by strength in the yen and Japan's stock markets. \par \par \uc2  The overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 3.75%, down from 5.00% late Monday. The three-month rate is 7.625%, down from 7.875%. Hong Kong's discount rate is quoted at 6.75%, down from 6.88% Monday. The markets were closed for a public holiday Tuesday. For more news, please refer to Telerate page [1085]. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the interbank market was being underpinned by a strong yen, which hit Y127.88 to the U.S. dollar Wednesday, and on Japan's stock market, which ended the session up 803.97 points, or 6.2%. The gains follow the submission of a bill that would allow the use of public funds to recapitalize Japanese banks. \par \par \uc2  "If you look at the ... Nikkei, the rallying yen, and the (Hong Kong) discount rate, everyone is in a good mood," said a dealer at a British bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said banks didn't expect any major surprises from Hong Kong Chief Executive Tung Chee-hwa's policy address late Wednesday, but expected him to reiterate the government's commitment to maintaining its 15-year-old \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg with the U.S. dollar, and to the free market, despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August. \par \par \uc2  Late Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is quoted at HK$7.7465 against the U.S. dollar, compared with HK$7.7481 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  In the futures market, the December three-month Hibor contract is quoted at 92.00, for an underlying money market rate of 8%, on a turnover of 1,044 lots. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 07-10-98 \par \par \uc2  0914GMT \par \par \uc2  1085 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010920dua70040t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
