\par\par \b \uc2  HK rates steady, market relaxed ahead long weekend. \b0\par\par\uc2 829 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 1998\par 06:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab Midday\tab      Open\tab \tab Previous Close\par HK$ SPOT    7.7483/93\tab   7.7480/90\tab  7.7482/92\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  FORWARDS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 3-Month\tab 520-560\tab     500-550\tab    540-580\par 6-Month    1,300-1,400\tab 1,200-1,400     1,250-1,450\par 1-Year     3,300-3,400\tab 3,200-3,500     3,200-3,400\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INTERBANK RATE (IN PERCENTAGE)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overnight  5.81-6.31\tab   5.50-5.75\tab  5.25-5.75\par 3-Month    7.81-8.12\tab   7.68-8.00\tab  7.62-8.12\par 6-Month    8.50-9.00\tab   8.50-8.75\tab  8.50-9.00\par 1-year     8.75-9.37\tab   8.75-9.25\tab  9.12-9.62\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Sept 30 (Reuters) - US/HK forwards and interbank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates were rangebound by midday on Wednesday in thin trade,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the market shrugging off news of a U.S. rate cut, dealers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Local money market traders were unsurprised by the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FOMC voting for a 25 basis point cut in the Fed fund rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Hong Kong money rates were rangebound. The overnight rate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was slightly firmer on long-weekend demand, but still lower\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par than the base rate at the new discount window of 6.88 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      Trading was quiet and dealers said they did not expect\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overseas speculators to make any major moves during the long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weekend. Hong Kong financial markets close on October 1 and 2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for Chinese National day holidays.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Many hedge funds had cut their long dollar position in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forwards and interest rate swaps over the past two weeks," a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealer at a major bank said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Many had been forced to square positions in both the equity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets as Hong Kong banks reduced credit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lines to hedge funds after the crisis at Long-Term Capital\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Management caused market jitters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Open interest in Hang Seng Index futures has declined\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sharply in the past few weeks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Gross open interest in Hang Seng Index future contracts is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par now around 88,594 contracts, compared with some 111,000\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par contracts in August.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A decline in open interest could imply more players had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par squared their positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Forwards market was less transparent, but traders said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par there were indications that more funds had cut their positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stock and futures exchange markets in August to foil\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par speculators it said had attacked the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peg.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Rates have fallen sharply since early September after the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HKMA announced moves to boost interbank liquidity, forcing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par speculators to cut their long dollar positions in forwards.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said they would expect market activity to continue\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to dwindle towards the year-end.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "I would not expect a large new position to be built before\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the end of the year," said one dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -Angi Li (852) 2847 4039; Fax 2845 0636.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Sept 30 (Reuters) - US/HK forwards and interbank rates were rangebound by midday on Wednesday in thin trade, with the market shrugging off news of a U.S. rate cut, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Local money market traders were unsurprised by the U.S. FOMC voting for a 25 basis point cut in the Fed fund rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hong Kong money rates were rangebound. The overnight rate was slightly firmer on long-weekend demand, but still lower than the base rate at the new discount window of 6.88 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Trading was quiet and dealers said they did not expect overseas speculators to make any major moves during the long weekend. Hong Kong financial markets close on October 1 and 2 for Chinese National day holidays.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Many hedge funds had cut their long dollar position in forwards and interest rate swaps over the past two weeks," a dealer at a major bank said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Many had been forced to square positions in both the equity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets as Hong Kong banks reduced credit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lines to hedge funds after the crisis at Long-Term Capital\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Management caused market jitters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Open interest in Hang Seng Index futures has declined\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sharply in the past few weeks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Gross open interest in Hang Seng Index future contracts is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par now around 88,594 contracts, compared with some 111,000\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par contracts in August.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A decline in open interest could imply more players had squared their positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Forwards market was less transparent, but traders said there were indications that more funds had cut their positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily in the stock and futures exchange markets in August to foil speculators it said had attacked the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peg.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Rates have fallen sharply since early September after the HKMA announced moves to boost interbank liquidity, forcing speculators to cut their long dollar positions in forwards.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said they would expect market activity to continue to dwindle towards the year-end.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I would not expect a large new position to be built before the end of the year," said one dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - Angi Li (852) 2847 4039; Fax 2845 0636.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du9u010gk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
