\par\par \b \uc2  US/HK forwards steady at open, factors in rate cut. \b0\par\par\uc2 445 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 1998\par 05:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab   Open\tab \tab Previous Close\par HK$ SPOT     7.7480/90\tab  7.7482/92\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  FOREWARDS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 3-Month     500-550\tab    540-580\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 6-Month     1,200-1,400     1,250-1,450\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1-Year\tab 3,200-3,500     3,200-3,400\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INTERBANK RATE (IN PERCENTAGE)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overnight   5.50-5.75\tab  5.25-5.75\par 3-Month     7.68-8.00\tab  7.62-8.12\par 6-Month     8.50-8.75\tab  8.50-9.00\par 1-year\tab 8.75-9.25\tab  9.12-9.62.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Sept 30 (Reuters) - US/HK forwards were mostly steady with the local money market showing little reaction to a U.S. rate cut, dealers said on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market was unsurprised by the U.S. FOMC voting for a 25 basis point cut in the Fed fund rate, leaving Hong Kong money rates range bound.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the base rate at the new discount window was lower at 6.88 percent from Tuesday's level of seven percent in response to the U.S. rate cut.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Despite a lower base rate, short term rates still held firm on the back of month-end demand as well as ahead of the long weekend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hong Kong financial markets will be closed on October 1 and and 2 for Chinese National day holidays.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said they did not expect overseas speculators to make any major moves during the long weekend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The overall atmosphere just does not favour speculative short positions against the Hong Kong dollar. Some major hedge funds have gradually squared their long dollar positions because of their liquidity problems," a dealer at a major bank said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Open interest in Hang Seng Index futures has declined sharply over the past few weeks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Gross open interest in Hang Seng Index future contracts is currently at around 88,594 contracts. This compared with some 111,000 contracts in August.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily in the stock and futures markets in August to foil speculators it said had attacked the Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peg with the aim of pushing up interest rates and share prices down to take profits on short positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A decline in open interest could imply more players had squared their positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Rates have fallen sharply since early September after the HKMA announced moves to boost interbank liquidity, forcing speculators to cut their long dollar position in forwards.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market activity was expected to dwindle towards the year end and an easier U.S. dollar interest rate could also help to reduce selling pressure on the Hong Kong dollar, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - Angi Li (852) 2847 4039; Fax 2845 0636.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du9u00zfo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
