\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar A Touch Weaker Late As Three-Month Rate Falls \b0\par\par\uc2 297 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 1998\par 11:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is a touch weaker late Tuesday, after the key three-month interbank lending rate fell during the session, but remains range-bound ahead of the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee meeting. \par \par \uc2  Around 0845 GMT (4:45 a.m. EDT), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7487 against the U.S. dollar, weaker than the HK$7.7485 quoted late Monday. The local unit has traded between HK$7.7480 and HK$7.7485 so far Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  It weakened after the benchmark three-month Hong Kong interbank offered rate fell to 8.00%, from 8.50% in the previous session, but is hugging a narrow trading band. \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the six-month premium edged up, on what dealers said was position-squaring ahead of the FOMC meeting, while the three-month premium eased. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected a cut of 25 to 50 basis points in U.S. interest rates overnight. A substantial cut, if matched locally, could push the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  close to HK$7.7500 to the U.S. dollar, which is seen as a trigger point for defensive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the three-month premium is quoted at 570 points, down from 590 points previously. The six-month premium is quoted at 1,450 points, up from 1,425 previously. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong interbank offered rate is quoted at 5.375%, up from 5.25% late Monday. For more Hibor news, please refer to Telerate page [1085]. \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2802 7002; skennedy@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 29-09-98 \par \par \uc2  0921GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du9t08e21\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
