\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Weaker Late, Seen Vulnerable To U.S. Rate Cut \b0\par\par\uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 1998\par 11:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is a touch weaker late Monday but is still firmly range-bound in thin trade, undermined by interest rates at low levels. \par \par \uc2  Around 0920 GMT (4:20 a.m. EDT), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7490 against the U.S. dollar, compared with HK$7.7475 late Friday. The local unit has moved between HK$7.7475 and HK$7.7492 so far Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar has had a quiet session, with no big news to focus on and with the big players sidelined ahead of the Federal Open Market Committee meeting Tuesday, which is expected to lead to a rate cut. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a European bank said a substantial Fed rate cut, if matched locally, could push the local unit dangerously close to the key HK$7.7500 level. That's seen as the trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Separately, there's less interest in the Hong Kong dollar now that speculators appear to have pulled back from the Hong Kong market, said a British dealer. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the September Hang Seng Index futures contract narrowed its discount to the cash market, alleviating the fears of those worried that speculators might again target the local unit through shorting the stock market and futures. \par \par \uc2  In the forward market, the three-month premium is at 590 points, from 570 points previously. The six-month premium is at 1,500 points, up from 1,420 previously. \par \par \uc2  Investors are unwinding their Hong Kong dollar hedges as they move out of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2802 7002; skennedy@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 28-09-98 \par \par \uc2  0942GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du9s08clv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
