\par\par \b \uc2  IMF sees risks from HK stock market  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 1998\par 19:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON, Sept 21 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its stock markets poses a number of risks, but the authorities there are competent and strongly committed to their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, a senior IMF official said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Charles Adams, deputy chief economist of the International Monetary Fund, said \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  could face the problem of stopping \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  once it had got under way. \par \par \uc2  "There is a risk of propping up the market and the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  get bigger and bigger and eventually you have to have an exit strategy," he told reporters after a news conference. \par \par \uc2  He noted that Hong Kong was also changing some elements of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board, a rigid system which pegs the Hong Kong dollar to the greenback. \par \par \uc2  "The political commitment to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system is very very strong; they have taken incredible pains so far," he said, describing the Hong Kong authorities as "very competent people...under amazing pressure." \par \par \uc2  He added: "I think the bigger risk for them is that if the situation in the rest of Asia does not improve soon then the situation is going to be very tough in that part of the world." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , effectively the territory's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in stock and futures markets last month to squeeze out speculators who had attacked the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  The moves prompted speculation that the territory was softening its tough free market stance in the face of financial problems across Asia. \par \par \uc2  ((Washington newsroom, +1 202 898-8310, fax +1 202 898-8383, washington.economic.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9l01jx9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
