\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals dither as dlr drags feet. \b0\par\par\uc2 766 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 1998\par 10:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0815 GMT - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were little changed in \par \par \uc2  slow trade as the dollar pulled off its lows against the yen \par \par \uc2  following falls in Tokyo stocks and Japanese interest rates. \par \par \uc2      Active yen sales against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  indirectly \par \par \uc2  supported dollar/yen, but its rise was capped by lingering \par \par \uc2  worries over Latin American economies and profit-taking by \par \par \uc2  Japanese investors before the end-September book closings. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo stocks closed at their lowest level in more than 12 \par \par \uc2  years as concerns over the banking system and a surge in \par \par \uc2  government bonds sucked money out of the market. \par \par \uc2  Fed chairman Alan Greenspan told the House Banking \par \par \uc2  Committee on Wednesday, that there was no concerted effort \par \par \uc2  among the Group of Seven nations to coordinate rate cuts. \par \par \uc2  He also said the financial crisis that began in Asia was \par \par \uc2  continuing to fuel deflationary pressures and that such forces \par \par \uc2  were moving towards the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  *** Bank Negara Malaysia said it might exempt senior \par \par \uc2  executives of companies with regional headquarters in Malaysia \par \par \uc2  from having to declare the amounts of money they carry when \par \par \uc2  crossing the border. \par \par \uc2  Assistant \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Awang Adek Hussin said the \par \par \uc2  bank was reviewing requests from Malaysian-based regional \par \par \uc2  firms. He said the penalty for violating recently imposed curbs \par \par \uc2  was a three-year jail sentence or a 10,000 ringgit fine, or \par \par \uc2  both. \par \par \uc2      The Consumer Price Index for August rose 5.6 percent \par \par \uc2  year-on-year after a 5.8 percent yearly rise in July. \par \par \uc2      *** China's trade minister said Beijing would continue to \par \par \uc2  seek the stability of the yuan against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and he \par \par \uc2  was certain China could achieve eight percent GDP growth this \par \par \uc2  year. \par \par \uc2  *** \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  Financial Secretary Donald Tsang defended the \par \par \uc2  government's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  local stock and futures \par \par \uc2  markets, saying it had no other option. \par \par \uc2  His comments followed overnight criticism from Greenspan \par \par \uc2  who said Hong Kong's efforts to boost share prices by using its \par \par \uc2  reserves to buy stock could not succeed and would damage its \par \par \uc2  credibility. \par \par \uc2      *** The rupiah was down at the 11,000 per dollar level but \par \par \uc2  business was thin. \par \par \uc2      Indonesia's justice minister said former president Suharto, \par \par \uc2  whose family and associates built up fortunes during his \par \par \uc2  32-year rule, could face jail if found guilty of abuse of \par \par \uc2  power. \par \par \uc2  It is the first time the government has said Suharto might \par \par \uc2  go to prison. Justice Minister Muladi said the government was \par \par \uc2  setting up a second team to look into Suharto's assets, \par \par \uc2  focussing on those allegedly stashed overseas. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin said on Wednesday that \par \par \uc2  Indonesia remained in difficulty because it "simply did not \par \par \uc2  take ownership of reform." \par \par \uc2      Following Malaysia's imposition of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls there is \par \par \uc2  persistent talk that Indonesia will go down the same road. \par \par \uc2      But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and government have repeatedly denied \par \par \uc2  that such a move was being planned. \par \par \uc2      *** The Korean won was a shade softer but showed little \par \par \uc2  reaction to a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official's comment that the \par \par \uc2  government should be more careful in considering further \par \par \uc2  reductions in domestic interest rates, given the effect on \par \par \uc2  foreign capital flows. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market already shows signs of \par \par \uc2  instability due to the reverse trends between local and \par \par \uc2  international interest rates," said Kang Hyeong-moon, chief of \par \par \uc2  the bank's planning department. \par \par \uc2  The Finance Ministry said it would provide tax incentives \par \par \uc2  for foreign investment in the manufacturing sector from \par \par \uc2  November 17. \par \par \uc2  It said it would allow foreign investors to buy land for \par \par \uc2  plants in a 20-year installment and that the approval period \par \par \uc2  for plant construction would be reduced to a maximum of 30 days \par \par \uc2  from 45 currently. \par \par \uc2      Change on the day THU 17 0818GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7998.......3.8000.........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah.....10975.00.....10775.00........-1.82% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........40.63........40.77.........0.34% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........43.78........43.65........-0.30% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.7158.......1.7245.........0.51% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...34.552.......34.505........-0.14% \par \p