\par\par \b \uc2  HKMA Yam/ \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Reserves-2:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Didn't Deplete Much \b0\par\par\uc2 133 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 1998\par 12:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The government has enough reserves to prevent stock market manipulation and still back \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in circulation, Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chief Executive Joseph Yam said Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Yam told legislators that Hong Kong's reserves are "ample" and weren't depleted significantly by stock and futures market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August. \par \par \uc2  The quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief, however, didn't say how much the government spent on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and didn't release the reserve level for August. \par \par \uc2  Many Hong Kong market participants believe the government spent up to US$15.0 billion of its July-end US$96.5 billion in reserves to fight off speculators in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , stock and futures markets. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 17-09-98 \par \par \uc2  1043GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du9h0801b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
