\par\par \b \uc2  HK London stocks ease uninspired by Hang Seng, Dow. \b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 1998\par 17:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 14 (Reuters) - Hong Kong stocks in London eased in London, failing to mirror a 1.1 percent gain in the Hang Seng overnight and uninspired by advances in overseas stock markets, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "We started higher in London on the back of the rise in Hong Kong, but...there was no reason to keep the sentiment up, so we drifted off," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  He said investors were waiting for the next move from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA), which has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support share prices, with a dose of scepticism. \par \par \uc2  "What the HKMA has done of late has created more confusion than anything else," said another trader. \par \par \uc2  The HKMA said on Monday it would keep its guaranteed U.S. dollar conversion rate for banks at HK$7.75 to US $1 for at least six months. \par \par \uc2  The move was aimed at reassuring jittery \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, but \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers in Hong Kong said they were confused rather than reassured. \par \par \uc2  A press report quoting HKMA chief executive Joseph Yam as saying a shift in the conversion rate to HK$7.80 would happen "suddenly" and in the "short term" had sparked a wave of Hong Kong dollar selling. \par \par \uc2  In London, index heavyweight HSBC Holdings  fell HK$3.0 to HK$147.5 compared with its Hong Kong close. \par \par \uc2  The Hang Seng index gained 83.4 points to 7,661.9. The Hang Seng London reference index eased 0.7 percent to 7,604.9. \par \par \uc2  The September futures contract on the index traded 100 points higher at 7,480 but still at a discount to the cash market, indicating expectations of a downside trend. \par \par \uc2  ((Silvia Aloisi, London newsroom +44 171 542 8712 fax +44 171 583 3769, uk.stocks.news@reuters.com)) (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9e010i4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
