\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Seen Supported By HKMA As Banks Use Conversion Pledge \b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 1998\par 05:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar has weakened to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level and is being supported at HK$7.75 per U.S. dollar on steady buying by the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  early Monday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "I think our government is buying at that level," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they detected the outflow of about US$400.0 million Monday morning from Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, as several large international investment banks began taking advantage of the HKMA's HK$7.75 per dollar conversion guarantee offered earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at that level at 0300 GMT (11 p.m. EDT Sunday), weaker than late Friday's HK$7.7480, and the U.S. bank's dealer said he doesn't expect it to budge, with the HKMA believed to be buying the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at that level, which it called its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level earlier this month. The HKMA didn't have an immediate comment on its activities or the reported outflow, but typically doesn't comment on what it's doing in markets. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. bank's dealer said he believes one U.S. investment bank is behind the outflow, selling Hong Kong dollars at HK$7.75 on the expectation that the HKMA will adjust the conversion guarantee to HK$7.80 sometime soon. \par \par \uc2  "I just saw one investment (bank) keep buying the outright 'TT,'" he said. \par \par \uc2  The bank may have been responding to an interview with HKMA Chief Executive Joseph Yam in the Hong Kong Economic Journal Monday. Yam elaborated on comments made earlier this month when he introduced measures to strengthen the Hong Kong dollar peg, saying he would move "shortly and suddenly" to change the conversion guarantee level to HK$7.80. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 14-09-98 \par \par \uc2  0323GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du9e07uv7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
