\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Stronger Late Mon -2: No Need To Move Swiftly \b0\par\par\uc2 354 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 1998\par 11:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The HKMA said it wouldn't move swiftly to change its guaranteed conversion level, fearing that would be misinterpreted as a devaluation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also noted that it won't move until the market exchange rate is "consistently at a level stronger than HK$7.75" and that it wanted to allow time for banks to remove hedge and stop-loss orders around HK$7.75. \par \par \uc2  Shortly after the news of the clarification hit the market, the spot Hong Kong dollar strengthened to HK$7.7470. It had been holding at HK$7.75 due to repeated HKMA local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying. That's well-known in markets here, as HK$7.75 is the HKMA's self-stated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level. \par \par \uc2  As pressure eased on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, interbank interest rates fell, along with forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums. \par \par \uc2  The three-month premium is 1,050 points above the spot rate, down from 1,250 points earlier Monday, but still above late Friday's 800 points. The six-month premiums is at 2,200 points, down from 2,500 points earlier in the day, but up from late Friday's 2,000 points. \par \par \uc2  The head of treasury at a domestic bank said market calm appeared to have been restored late in Hong Kong, but that an outflow of funds may be repeated by London traders overnight. \par \par \uc2  He said the HKMA bought itself some time by saying it isn't moving swiftly to change the guaranteed bank conversion rate, but that speculators may already be focusing beyond the six-month period and hedging accordingly before then as they position themselves to strain the Hong Kong dollar peg. \par \par \uc2  He said Hong Kong dollar selling wasn't as panicked as it was two Fridays ago, when unfounded rumors of capital control measures that would be imposed on the Hong Kong dollar sparked a scramble for banks looking to cover short customer positions. \par \par \uc2  -by Adam S. Najberg; (852)2802-7002; naj@asiaonline.net \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 14-09-98 \par \par \uc2  0906GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du9e07vq0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
