\par\par \b \uc2  HKMA's Carse says ready to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 259 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 1998\par 18:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON, Sept 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Chief Executive David Carse said Friday the HKMA was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock and futures markets to counter any market manipulation. \par \par \uc2  "If we feel that the assets markets are being manipulated then we would step in," Carse told reporters in Washington. "We do not rule out future \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  government began buying stocks and futures last month, saying it wanted to foil speculative attacks on the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  Earlier this month the HKMA announced measures intended to strengthen the territory's linked exchange rate system and reduce interest rate volatility. The measures included specific rules for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  conversion and moves meant to bolster liquidity. \par \par \uc2  Carse said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not designed to "prop up" the stock and futures markets, but rather to "squeeze speculators." \par \par \uc2  Carse said measures to beef up Hong Kong financial markets were not a breach of Hong Kong's free market principles. "The controls are really trying to deal with market abuses which were occurring." \par \par \uc2  "I would hope that the follow-up measures that we've announced, in terms of tightening up on short-selling, increasing the disclosure in both the cash market and the futures market, will reduce the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the future," Carse said after giving a speech at a conference hosted by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation. \par \par \uc2  ((Washington newsroom, +1 202 898-8317, fax +1 202 898-8383, washington.economic.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9b00zry\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
