\par\par \b \uc2  Hong Kong to maintain  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  board - official. \b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 1998\par 18:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON, Sept 11 (Reuters) - Hong Kong intends to maintain its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system and the current link to the U.S. dollar, Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Chief Executive David Carse said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Hong Kong remains determined to maintain the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system and the present link between the Hong Kong dollar and U.S. dollar," Carse said in a speech to a conference here. \par \par \uc2  Carse defended HKMA's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock and futures markets, saying it was designed to counter market manipulation and speculation. \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "not designed to prop up the stock and futures market." Carse added the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "not a breach of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's free market principles." \par \par \uc2  Rather, he said the HKMA was demonstrating its determination to protect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stability of Hong Kong's monetary system. \par \par \uc2  Carse said 1998 and 1999 would be tough years for Hong Kong banks because of increased bad debt and lower operating profits. \par \par \uc2  "However, lower profitability in itself is not a cause for concerns in terms of systemic stability because banks remain highly capitalised and liquid," Carse said. "What we are facing is a profitability issue not a solvency issue. Banks should be able to manage there way through the current difficulties." \par \par \uc2  Carse said problem loans have risen as a result of the regional crisis and the slowdown in the domestic economy. \par \par \uc2  "However, while asset quality is getting worse, it is not collapsing," he told a Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation conference. \par \par \uc2  ((Washington newsroom, +1 202 898-8317, fax +1 202 898-8383, washington.economic.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9b00xwy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
