\par\par \b \uc2  HKMA's Carse/Dlr Peg -2: No Breach of Free-Mkt Tradition \b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 1998\par 18:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  regards its recent stock-market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  not as a breach of its vaunted free-market principles but as a signal to speculators that it will defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  whatever the cost, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said Friday. \par \par \uc2  David Carse, deputy chief executive of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told a gathering of bank supervisors here that speculative attacks on the Hong Kong dollar have driven up interest rates and caused stock prices to plummet nearly 50% over the last year. \par \par \uc2  But the territory's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no intention of abandoning its fixed exchange-rate system, among the last of its kind in East Asia. "Hong Kong remains firmly determined to maintain the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -board system and the link between the Hong Kong dollar and the U.S. dollar, and we're prepared to accept the pain of adjustment," he said. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -board system requires a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ensure that the total of a country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in circulation and banking reserves always equals the amount of its foreign reserves. Under such a system, when capital flows out of the country, interest rates automatically rise. Hong Kong's interest rates used to match U.S. rates, Carse said, but are now about two percentage points higher because of the Asian financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  Carse said speculators have been using a "double-play" strategy to attack that system, obligating the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to spend an estimated $10 billion of its foreign reserves on stock-market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The strategy involves selling \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars and shorting \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  stocks. The pressure on the dollar causes interest rates to rise and causes stock prices to fall, so speculators can make money whether or not the dollar loses value. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "That's the reason we've been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the stock and futures\par market," Carse said. "The objective is not to prop up stocks and\par futures....The objective is to squeeze speculators." Accordingly, the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are "not a breach of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's free-market principles,\par because the objective is not to support the market per se," he said.\par -By Joseph Rebello; 202-862-9279; e-mail:\par joseph.rebello@cor.dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 11-09-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1615GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4215 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du9b07ur5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
