\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Stronger Midday On U.S. Dlr Short-Selling \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 1998\par 06:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is a touch stronger midday Wednesday as investors sell the U.S. dollar short against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in moderate amounts. \par \par \uc2  They're doing that because while the overnight and one-week Hong Kong interbank rates are below comparable U.S. dollar rates, longer-term local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates are above them, making Hong Kong dollar positions more attractive, said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar is trading at HK$7.7490 per US$1.00 at 0350 GMT (11:50 p.m. EDT, Tuesday), compared with HK$7.7495 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums are mostly flat, with the pick-up in Hong Kong dollar buying indicating participants are feeling better about the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and aren't taking on new positions. Many are closing out their hedging positions as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthens. \par \par \uc2  The three-month forward premium is 610 points over the spot rate, scarcely changed from 600 points late Tuesday. The six-month premium is down to 1,650 points from 1,800 points. \par \par \uc2  While investors continue to sell short-term Hong Kong dollars to benefit from higher U.S. dollar interest rates, market participants don't intend to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to HK$7.75, a level at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to halt the U.S. dollar's rise. \par \par \uc2  At the same time, short-selling of U.S. dollars in longer-term money markets is providing a push in the opposite direction and should keep the Hong Kong dollar a touch stronger from Tuesday's levels. \par \par \uc2  "Over one week to two weeks, people like to short the (U.S.) dollar against the Hong Kong (dollar)," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  -By Adam S. Najberg; (852)2802-7002; naj@asiaonline.net \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 09-09-98 \par \par \uc2  0417GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du9907pmc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
