\par\par \b \uc2  WEEKAHEAD - HK markets seen wary after peg measures. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Alison Leung \par \uc2 781 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 1998\par 10:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Sept 6 (Reuters) - Hong Kong financial markets will focus this week on steps by authorities to bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, action analysts said may help stabilise interest rates but could also create more uncertainty. \par \par \uc2  "It's evidence of further uncertainty and a lack of confidence in the peg mechanism," said Andrew Ballingal, a strategist at Schroders Asia. \par \par \uc2  The weekend moves by the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) to bolster the local dollar's link to the U.S. dollar follows recent government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in stocks and futures aimed at fending off speculators. \par \par \uc2  "(HKMA chief) Joseph Yam should listen to what Milton Friedman has to say," Ballingal said. \par \par \uc2  Friedman, an economist famous for his free-market, anti-government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  theories, told the Asian Wall Street Journal on Thursday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  government's huge \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock market undermined the credibility of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system. \par \par \uc2  Others agreed. \par \par \uc2  "I believe what the government is trying to do is pursue the Singaporean model, more than anything else. We believe it is a negative thing," said one analyst who asked not to be named. \par \par \uc2  On Saturday the HKMA announced new measures to strengthen the territory's linked exchange rate system and reduce interest rate volatility. \par \par \uc2  The measures, which officials described as purification of Hong Kong's 15 year-old \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, included new rules for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  conversion and moves meant to bolster liquidity. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that in the short term, the market expected lower interest rates. But despite the likely benefits of potentially lower interest rates to the stock market, the main issue was perception, they said. \par \par \uc2  "Like anything to do with markets, it's something that requires confidence, the actions of the authorities bely that," Ballingal said. \par \par \uc2  "It's sentiment driven, if this does not work, or if the (interest rate) volatility does not change, you will see a problem," he said. \par \par \uc2  Fears linger that the government may still \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's blue chips are expected to be rangebound this coming week, particularly after the futures and stock exchanges tightened regulations last week. \par \par \uc2  Alex Tang, research director at Core Pacific - Yamaichi International (HK), said as speculators gradually retreated from the Hong Kong market, trading could steady. \par \par \uc2  "Speculators are moving out from the market since they know that it is difficult to win the game as the government changes its goalposts frequently," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong Futures Exchange last week imposed a special margin surcharge on Hang Seng Index futures and options positions exceeding 10,000 contracts and tightened reporting rules requiring members to disclose positions of 250 contracts instead of 500 previously. \par \par \uc2  It said it would also ask members to identify the holders of large positions. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong Stock Exchange also took steps last week, announcing that it would reinstate the tick rule from Monday, banning short sales of shares below the best current ask price. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the moves were part of the government's efforts to enhance \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resilience to speculative attacks, after stock market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in which the government is estimated to have spent some HK$120 billion (US$15 billion). \par \par \uc2  But the moves could reduce trading interest, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The point is why should anybody come in right now? They can't hedge their positions." said Peter Churchouse, managing director at Morgan Stanley Dean Witter Asia. \par \par \uc2  The blue chip index surged 169.88 points, or 2.32 percent, to close at 7,488.47 on Friday but fell 341.27 points, or 4.35 percent, over the week. \par \par \uc2  September index futures jumped 210 points, to close at 7,170 points on Friday, a 318 point discount to the spot index. \par \par \uc2  Tang said he expected the Hang Seng index to see some resistance at 7,500 to 7,800 points. "The government has a number of short positions in September futures and they will buy back futures to support the market above 7,000," he said. \par \par \uc2  Left to its own devices the Hang Seng Index would fall below 6,000 points over the next few weeks, said Churchouse. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said China plays could be the focus of trading next week following a strong rebound in H-shares and red chips on Friday as a firming yen eased pressures on the Chinese yuan. \par \par \uc2  The H-share index jumped 35.59 points, or 13.35 percent to 302.21 on Friday and the red chip index rose 88.88 points, or 14.95 percent, to close at 683.55. ($HK$7.75) \par \par \uc2  - Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6369; Fax (852) 2845 0636 \par \par \uc2  - Email: hongkong.newsroomzreuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021217du9600uiv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
