\par\par \b \uc2  HK Legislator Criticizes Govt Financial  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 1998\par 22:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (AP)--Government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up share prices has damaged the territory's reputation as a free-market financial center, a legislator said Sunday. \par \par \uc2  Independent lawmaker Emily Lau said on Radio \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  that the stakes in the government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  stretch far beyond the stock market. \par \par \uc2  "With financial turmoil sweeping around the world, the Hong Kong dollar is seen as one of the vulnerable candidates for the next collapse," she said. \par \par \uc2  Last month, the government spent 15% of its $96 billion foreign reserves on a two-week stock buying spree to lift share prices to levels where speculators suffered heavy losses. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  also announced steps on Saturday to strengthen the territory's 15-year-old \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Lau said the battle for the Hong Kong dollar is a "political test as well as a financial crisis." \par \par \uc2  She warned that as market volatility continues and the people find that little has been achieved by the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they may become "restive and even angry." \par \par \uc2  "Loss of public confidence would endanger the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg to the U.S. dollar, which is the linchpin of our financial system," she added. \par \par \uc2  Speculators have played on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg's connection to local interest rates to drive rates higher and share prices lower, in an attempt to weaken the peg, which is set at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 06-09-98 \par \par \uc2  2001GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du9607mna\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
