\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-HKMA unveils moves to strengthen HK dlr peg. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Andrea Ricci \par \uc2 756 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 1998\par 13:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Sept 5 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) on Saturday unveiled a series of new measures to strengthen the territory's linked exchange rate system and reduce interest rate volatility. \par \par \uc2  The measures, which officials described as a purification of Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, included new rules for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  conversion and moves meant to bolster liquidity. \par \par \uc2  "These measures aim at strengthening Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board arrangements and achieving an even higher degree of transparency and disclosure," HKMA chief executive Joseph Yam told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  The measures would make Hong Kong's 15-year-old \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, which pegs the Hong Kong dollar to the U.S. dollar, less susceptible to manipulation and could reduce the need for government stock market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the stock and futures markets in August to foil speculators who had attacked the Hong Kong dollar with the aim of driving interest rates up and stock prices down to take profits on short stock positions. \par \par \uc2  As part of its new measures, the HKMA replaced its Liquidity Adjustment Facility (LAF) with a discount window with a single Base Rate rather than a bid-offer spread used under the LAF, reducing the authority's discretion to affect rates. \par \par \uc2  The HKMA removed most restrictions on repeated borrowings from the discount window. \par \par \uc2  The restrictions were put in place last year to make it more difficult for speculators to fund attacks on the Hong Kong dollar but had the unwanted effect of squeezing liquidity as banks avoided the LAF for fear of being penalised. \par \par \uc2  The HKMA said no new issues of paper other than government Exchange Fund bills and notes backed by foreign reserves would be accepted as collateral at the discount window. Currently, some other highly rated debt securities are eligible. \par \par \uc2  Allowing freer access to day-end liquidity through the use of the Exchange Fund paper fully backed by foreign reserves would dampen interest rate volatility without departing from the discipline of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board arrangement, the HKMA said. \par \par \uc2  To that end, the authority said it would issue new Exchange Fund paper only when there was an inflow of of funds, assuring that all new paper would be fully backed by foreign reserves. \par \par \uc2  Yam said the measures would make it much more difficult for speculators to attack the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  Liquidity as represented by the aggregate balance in the banking system currently is less than HK$2 billion, making it easy for speculators to boost interest rates with small outlays. \par \par \uc2  With some HK$96 billion of Exchange Fund paper outstanding, liquidity is potentially much greater, Yam said. \par \par \uc2  "Speculators would probably need to short about HK$30 billion before interest rates go sharply higher, sending the stock market down," he said. \par \par \uc2  The HKMA will publish a Base Rate every day starting from Monday. The rate would be market sensitive, but the methodology for determining the rate still needed to be honed, Yam said. \par \par \uc2  He suggested an average of the overnight and one-month Hong Kong interbank rates might be used as a reference initially. \par \par \uc2  The authority said it stood ready to convert Hong Kong dollars in the clearing accounts of licensed banks into U.S. dollars at a fixed exchange rate of HK$7.75 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The move "purified" the system because by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board rules, aggregate balances as one of the liabilities of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board should be transferable into U.S. dollars. \par \par \uc2  "The rules of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board say that you have to convert your liabilities into U.S. dollars," Yam said. \par \par \uc2  The authority chose 7.75, rather than the peg rate of 7.78, because it was closer to the current market level and has been an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  point for the HKMA. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was linked to the U.S. dollar at a rate of HK$7.8 per US$1 in 1983. It is permitted to trade in a narrow band around that level and typically trades on the strong side. \par \par \uc2  "If all of a sudden when the market rate is near 7.75, you remove that support to 7.78, then all these stop losses will be triggered and there will be volatility," said Yam. \par \par \uc2  The HKMA intended to change its convertibility undertaking to 7.80 when the spot rate strengthened, he said. \par \par \uc2  - Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6371; Fax (852) 2845-0636 \par \par \uc2  - hongkong.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021217du9500u32\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
