\par\par \b \uc2  Hong Kong poised to review financial market rules. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kathleen Kearney \par \uc2 641 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 1998\par 16:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Sept 4 (Reuters) - Measures to beef up Hong Kong financial markets, prevent excessive speculation in stocks and futures and protect the local dollar will top the agenda at a meeting between the administration and legislators on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Financial Secretary Donald Tsang will face legislators at the meeting of the legislature's Financial Affairs Panel, an aide to panel chairman Ambrose Lau said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "There are three items on the agenda. Government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the SFC (Securities and Futures Commission) report and insider dealing," the aide said. \par \par \uc2  Legislators have said they would question Tsang over the government's recent huge \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock market and criticise the government's use of an estimated HK$100 billion or more of its foreign exchanges reserves. \par \par \uc2  Tsang was widely expected to use the session to propose new measures to safeguard the health of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  financial markets and limit excessive speculation. \par \par \uc2  The government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which officials have argued was aimed at protecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, sent shockwaves around the world and caused deep concern in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the administration would need legislators' support in possible rule changes concerning the Hong Kong dollar forwards market, strengthening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board, circuit breakers for the stock and futures markets and closer monitoring of Hang Seng Index futures trade. \par \par \uc2  However, experts warned against overly draconian measures, especially those governing short selling. \par \par \uc2  "It will just drive the business offshore anyway," executive director Nicholas Clement-Jones at SBC Warburg Dillon Read said. \par \par \uc2  Short selling of Hong Kong listed stocks was not permitted until 1993, but was often done outside Hong Kong or over-the-counter. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think that we need a radical overhaul of the way this town does business and the regulatory regime under which that business is conducted," Clement-Jones said. \par \par \uc2  The Stock Exchange of Hong Kong and the Hong Kong Futures Exchange said on Friday they were not aware of the content of the government's Monday presentation and had not been asked by the government to make changes to any of their rules. \par \par \uc2  Both exchanges have made small but important changes since trading on August 27 and 28 when huge government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock and futures markets raised turnover on the stock exchange to HK$22.97 billion and a record HK$79.00 billion respectively. \par \par \uc2  Last Saturday, the futures exchange announced increases in the cost of holding large open positions in Hang Seng Index futures, a favourite investment instrument of hedge funds. \par \par \uc2  It imposed a special margin surcharge of 150 percent on all Hang Seng Index futures and options positions exceeding 10,000 contracts from the close of trading on Tuesday, September 1. \par \par \uc2  The stock exchange council on Wednesday said it would reinstate the uptick rule on short selling and require short sales to be made at the best current ask price. \par \par \uc2  While the battle has been expressly aimed at protecting the Hong Kong dollar, it has sparked heated rows in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief executive Joseph Yam has criticised the Hongkong Securities Clearing Co Ltd for extending a grace period to brokers who could not settle trades transacted on Thursday and Friday, some of whom were suspected to have been involved in illegal short selling. \par \par \uc2  By giving the grace period, the clearing house was seen in some quarters as having scuppered the authority's aim to hurt speculators by forcing them to pay the highest market prices or high borrowing rates for stock lending. \par \par \uc2  The clearing company said it regularly allowed a grace period of one and sometimes two days to brokers and international funds who were unable to retrieve stock from the depth of a custodian banks' vaults in the permitted two days after a transaction. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021217du9400sz3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
