\par\par \b \uc2  HK  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  hastens re-peg need - WI Carr. \b0\par\par\uc2 611 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 1998\par 13:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Sept 2 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local stock market has intensified the need for a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation, Michael Taylor, chief economist at Indosuez W.I. Carr Securities, said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Taylor said he did not expect a devaluation in Hong Kong before one in mainland China, which was most likely early next year. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently moved to defend the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from speculators by spending an estimated HK$100 billion ($12.8 billion) on stocks and futures contracts. \par \par \uc2  "Having forfeited the assumption of transparency, Hong Kong will have to reconstruct without the cash that was attracted to the promise of that transparency," Taylor said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  "Even under the best scenarios Hong Kong dollar assets and Hong Kong dollar debt will now be priced accordingly. There is a relationship between the amount of creditability blown in the defence, and the level to which asset prices must adjust," he said. \par \par \uc2  Speaking to reporters, Taylor said Hong Kong asset prices were sure to fall further with deflationary forces taking hold the world over. Under current conditions, the pace of the fall was likely to be quite intense. \par \par \uc2  He said there was little chance Hong Kong interest rates would decline. The flight of foreign capital had kept, and would keep, interbank rates high, and local banks would be forced to raise retail lending rates because they could not endure painfully tight margins forever. \par \par \uc2  For the government, the best move would be to devalue the Hong Kong dollar either by re-pegging it straight away at a weaker rate or letting it float for a while to find a level and then re-pegging it. \par \par \uc2  "We expect that Hong Kong will be taking some of the adjustment through the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar has been linked to the U.S. dollar at a rate of HK$7.8 since 1983 and is permitted to float in a narrow band around that level. \par \par \uc2  Taylor said the goverment should devalue "the sooner the better". He said the government was likely to delay such a move until pressures on the economy became severe. \par \par \uc2  "Despite the fact that the government buying of the stock market appears to have stopped, devaluation in the very near term is probably not going to happen, and will not happen until it is forced by the very intensity of deflationary forces at work," he said. \par \par \uc2  Taylor said he expected Hong Kong would wait for China to devalue, which it would do soon to help to support its reform programme in a continuing deflationary environment. \par \par \uc2  In an August research report, Indosuez W.I. Carr predicted China would devalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 20 percent around the turn of the year. \par \par \uc2  "My own expectation is that Hong Kong will wait for China's devaluation. I therefore expect the devaluation of the Hong Kong dollar before Chinese New Year (February 1999)," said Taylor. \par \par \uc2  Worries about the contagion effects of a Hong Kong dollar devaluation were exaggerated as were concerns about the effect on the territory's banking sector. \par \par \uc2  Taylor declined to estimate what would be a proper level for the Hong Kong dollar, saying it would depend on the level of confidence in the market. \par \par \uc2  "What level the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  goes to depends on what it takes to regain confidence in Hong Kong," he said. \par \par \uc2  Taylor rejected the idea of dollarising the Hong Kong economy, saying it "would sound an immediate death knell for local Hong Kong banks". \par \par \uc2  - Andrea Ricci (852) 2843-6371; Fax (852) 2845-0636 \par \par \uc2  - hongkong.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du92022la\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
